    <bpmn:process id="W_W1790" name="W1790. Growth Incentive &amp; New Store Opening Rebate Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store opening; annual growth target review
Frequency: ~10–15 new stores/year trigger new store rebates; annual growth assessment
Volume: ~50–100 vendors with growth/new store incentives
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, Category Managers, VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W1790 — Growth Incentive &amp; New Store Opening Rebate Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1790_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1790_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1790_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1790_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1790_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1790_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1790_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1790_Start3" name="New store opening; annual growth target review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1790_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1790_Task4" name="New store opening rebate: (a) key vendors provide per-store contribution toward…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: New store opening rebate: (a) key vendors provide per-store contribution toward opening costs (shelf fixtures, signage, initial stock discount), (b) typical structure: PHP 50K–500K per new store depending on vendor size and category, (c) triggered by proof of new store opening (photos, store certificate), (d) tracked per vendor per store opening
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Buyer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per new store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1790_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1790_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1790_Task5" name="Growth incentive: (a) vendor offers additional rebate if BuildRight&#x27;s purchases…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Growth incentive: (a) vendor offers additional rebate if BuildRight&#x27;s purchases grow X% year-over-year (e.g., 1% additional rebate for &gt; 10% growth), (b) system tracks YTD growth rate per vendor, (c) Category Manager assesses if growth target is achievable; adjusts procurement strategy if near target, (d) growth incentive accrual added to base rebate accrual per W1788
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1790_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1790_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1790_Task6" name="Claim submission: Category Manager compiles evidence of new store openings…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Claim submission: Category Manager compiles evidence of new store openings (certificate, photos, grand opening documentation); submits to vendor for rebate payment
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1790_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1790_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1790_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1790_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1790_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-358 (ensure controlled execution — Rebate Agreement &amp; Accrual Management (PA-39.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
