    <bpmn:process id="W_W1791" name="W1791. Special Pricing Agreement (SPA) Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: One-time special pricing request from vendor for specific customer/project
Frequency: ~200–300 SPAs/year
Volume: Primarily for B2B/project sales per VS-11
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Buyer, Sales Team, AP Manager
Source: workflow W1791 — Special Pricing Agreement (SPA) Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1791_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1791_Lane1" name="Sales Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1791_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1791_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1791_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1791_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1791_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1791_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1791_Lane4" name="AP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1791_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1791_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1791_Start6" name="One-time special pricing request from vendor for specific customer/project">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1791_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1791_Task7" name="Sales Team identifies project opportunity requiring special pricing: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sales Team identifies project opportunity requiring special pricing: (a) contractor tender for large project (e.g., 50-unit condominium), (b) government procurement bid, (c) competitive bid situation requiring below-SRP pricing
Responsible (R): Sales Team
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Per opportunity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1791_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1791_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1791_Task8" name="Category Manager negotiates SPA with vendor: (a) vendor provides special…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Manager negotiates SPA with vendor: (a) vendor provides special pricing for the specific project (below standard wholesale price), (b) BuildRight passes savings to customer (with margin retention), (c) SPA documented: vendor, product, quantity, special price, valid period, project reference, (d) entered in system as special pricing arrangement
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Buyer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1791_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1791_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1791_Task9" name="System applies SPA pricing when sales order matches SPA criteria (customer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System applies SPA pricing when sales order matches SPA criteria (customer, product, quantity, date); margin tracked separately to show BuildRight&#x27;s margin vs. vendor&#x27;s contribution
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1791_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1791_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1791_Task10" name="Post-project reconciliation: AP Manager reconciles SPA purchases to SPA…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-project reconciliation: AP Manager reconciles SPA purchases to SPA agreement; claims any volume or project completion rebates from vendor; settles SPA differential
Responsible (R): AP Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks post-project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1791_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1791_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1791_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1791_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1791_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-358 (ensure controlled execution — Rebate Agreement &amp; Accrual Management (PA-39.1).) | - operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
