    <bpmn:process id="W_W1792" name="W1792. Vendor Markdown Allowance &amp; Damage Claim Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Markdown event (seasonal clearance, damaged goods, quality issue)
Frequency: ~100–200 markdown allowance claims/year
Volume: ~PHP 30–50M in annual markdown allowances recovered from vendors
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Store Manager, AP Manager, Vendor
Source: workflow W1792 — Vendor Markdown Allowance &amp; Damage Claim Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1792_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1792_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1792_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1792_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1792_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1792_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1792_Lane3" name="Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1792_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1792_Lane4" name="AP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1792_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1792_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1792_Start6" name="Markdown event (seasonal clearance, damaged goods, quality issue)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1792_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1792_Task7" name="Markdown event triggered: (a) seasonal clearance (end-of-season items): vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Markdown event triggered: (a) seasonal clearance (end-of-season items): vendor agreement typically provides markdown money (vendor funds a portion of the discount), (b) damaged goods (in-transit or in-store damage): vendor provides credit if damage is their responsibility, (c) quality issue: defective product identified per VS-31; vendor provides markdown or return credit, (d) slow-moving inventory: vendor may provide markdown support to clear aged stock
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1792_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1792_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1792_Task8" name="Category Manager prepares markdown allowance claim: (a) list of affected SKUs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Manager prepares markdown allowance claim: (a) list of affected SKUs, quantities, original cost, proposed markdown, (b) vendor contribution requested (% of markdown cost), (c) justification (seasonal, damage, quality, slow-movement), (d) photos of damaged/defective items, (e) submit to vendor for approval
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1792_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1792_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1792_Task9" name="Vendor approves/denies claim: (a) if approved: vendor issues credit note or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor approves/denies claim: (a) if approved: vendor issues credit note or markdown allowance payment, (b) if partially approved: negotiate remaining amount, (c) if denied: Category Manager decides whether to absorb markdown cost or escalate to VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): Vendor / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1792_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1792_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1792_Task10" name="AP Manager records vendor markdown allowance: (a) credit note received from…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: AP Manager records vendor markdown allowance: (a) credit note received from vendor applied to AP balance, (b) or cash payment received from vendor, (c) markdown allowance reduces COGS (contra-COGS treatment), (d) remaining markdown cost (BuildRight&#x27;s share) recorded as markdown expense
Responsible (R): AP Manager
Accountable (A): Accounting Manager
Duration: Per claim</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1792_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1792_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1792_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1792_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1792_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-209 (ensure vendor rebate accuracy &amp; recognition.) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1792_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1792_Annotation12" targetRef="W1792_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
